KZ3 patch 2048 (rsx rounds 49-50): asynchronous PSO builds for the live renderer, LD_PSO_ASYNC (default on since
pass 50; LD_PSO_ASYNC=0 = the synchronous builds).
On a walker PSO miss the walker decompiles and looks the VS/PS blobs up (memory, then the disk cache) as before, then
queues the HLSL, render state and layout to worker threads (LD_PSO_ASYNC_THREADS, default 3) that compile the missing
blobs (D3DCompile) and create the PSO (through patch 2031's pipeline library). Until the build is back the key's PSO
entry is pending (pso NULL) and its draws are skipped (drop{pso}), as RPCS3's asynchronous shader mode does; the
walker merges finished builds at its next PSO lookup (blobs into the memory and disk caches, the key into
pso_keys.bin, the PSO into its entry). Pass 50: one in-flight compile per shader blob (the walker registers each
missing blob in a table keyed by type, hash, length and source; the first job compiles it, later jobs wait for it).
The bookkeeping is platform-neutral in libs/video/rsx_pso_async.h (host test tools/smoke/test_pso_async.c).
Aim: the cold-cache level-start stall (K4: 245 misses = 16.4 s of walker time, RSX pass 48).
Statistics: [pso-async] every 256 frames once builds ran.
